# Kept out of git, as the earlier studies' were: the recordings (snapshots and engine results), screenshots, judgment
# and destination caches, and image crops. data/recordings.json has the size and SHA-256 of every recording file, so a
# copy kept elsewhere (C:/Users/guilh/dev/rampa-study-recordings/round-5) can be checked before judgments are re-run on it.
pages/*/recording/
pages/*/*.png
pages/*/cache/
pages/*/cache-*/
pages/*/.rampa/
pages/*/*-collect.json
packets/*/
# Also kept out, as the precision-fixes notes kept them (study/notes-precision-fixes/compact.py): the full reports and
# the consoles. scripts/compact.py keeps in git the part of each report the analysis reads (pages/<slug>/*.judged.json:
# every judgment and rule finding, the model's suggestions, the criteria's summaries, the notes, the capture state and
# the usage); the full ones are in the recordings copy.
pages/*/report.json
pages/*/noconfirm-report.json
pages/*/cut090-report.json
pages/*/*console*.txt
# Attempts set aside (a connection drop, a rate limit): their logs are kept, not their recordings or caches.
pages/*/discarded-*/**/recording/
pages/*/discarded-*/**/*.png
pages/*/discarded-*/**/cache*/
pages/*/discarded-*/**/*-collect.json
pages/*/discarded-*/**/*report.json
scripts/__pycache__/
